{"lines": ["Start with the code that fell. On the eighth of November, 1969, the Zodiac killer mailed a card to the San Francisco Chronicle. Inside, a cipher of three hundred and forty characters. It is called Z340.", "For fifty-one years, nobody could solve it.", "On the fifth of December, 2020, it was read. By David Oranchak, an American software engineer. Sam Blake, an Australian mathematician. And Jarl Van Eycke, a Belgian programmer. Three private citizens, using a program Van Eycke had written, called AZdecrypt.", "The Zodiac had apparently made a mistake while building the cipher. That mistake made it harder to solve.", "And the message? It said he was not the man called Sam, who had phoned a television show. It said he was not afraid of the gas chamber. It gave no clue to who he was.", "Rule one. A code that beats you today may only be waiting for a better tool."], "words": [["Start", 0.0, 0.24], ["with", 0.24, 0.46], ["the", 0.46, 0.56], ["code", 0.56, 0.88], ["that", 0.88, 1.14], ["fell.", 1.14, 1.38], ["On", 2.2, 2.25], ["the", 2.25, 2.34], ["eighth", 2.34, 2.74], ["of", 2.74, 2.79], ["November,", 2.79, 3.1], ["1969,", 3.1, 4.44], ["the", 5.22, 5.38], ["Zodiac", 5.38, 5.86], ["killer", 5.86, 6.2], ["mailed", 6.2, 6.5], ["a", 6.5, 6.55], ["card", 6.55, 7.0], ["to", 7.0, 7.44], ["the", 7.44, 7.54], ["San", 7.54, 7.72], ["Francisco", 7.72, 8.36], ["Chronicle.", 8.36, 8.8], ["Inside,", 9.66, 10.04], ["a", 10.5, 10.66], ["cipher", 10.66, 11.06], ["of", 11.06, 11.34], ["three", 11.34, 11.415], ["hundred", 11.415, 11.49], ["and", 11.49, 11.565], ["forty", 11.565, 11.64], ["characters.", 11.64, 12.96], ["It", 13.88, 14.0], ["is", 14.0, 14.1], ["called", 14.1, 14.4], ["Z340.", 14.4, 15.26], ["For", 16.56, 16.98], ["fifty-one", 16.98, 17.38], ["years,", 17.38, 17.92], ["nobody", 18.32, 18.64], ["could", 18.64, 19.08], ["solve", 19.08, 19.44], ["it.", 19.44, 19.66], ["On", 20.4, 20.52], ["the", 20.52, 20.6], ["fifth", 20.6, 20.98], ["of", 20.98, 21.03], ["December,",